 # Zunévio native fork
 
-Prepared for PriceBond. Upstream: https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord
+Zunévio developer: Amit Hasan Sami. Public contact: amitsami110@gmail.com; GitHub: https://github.com/amitsami. Upstream: https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord
 Upstream commit: fe95bb60aa9cd205cf4ab8bd25a5bec71a595b4f
 
-This is a GPLv3 derivative fork, not a claim that PriceBond wrote the upstream code. Original source, copyright, licence, contributor acknowledgements and upstream documentation are retained. Review inherited third-party asset/font licences before a public release.
+This is a GPLv3 derivative fork, not a claim that Amit Hasan Sami wrote the upstream code. Original source, copyright, licence, contributor acknowledgements and upstream documentation are retained. Review inherited third-party asset/font licences before a public release.
 
 ## Native UI, not an HTML shell
 
 The Android and desktop applications keep BitChord's actual Compose UI, player engines, floating navigation, artwork transitions, lyric clock, word/letter sweep, queue, service integrations and native analysis code. They are not a WebView wrapping the design preview.
 
-Zunévio changes include distinct application/package identifiers, PriceBond publisher metadata, Z icons, visible/export branding, Glass enabled by default for new Android installs, and a translucent lyric capsule connected to the actual player backdrop in both portrait and landscape layouts. Reduced-blur settings and unsupported-device fallbacks remain in place. Saved user preferences are not overwritten. Lyrics need a provider with word timestamps for the native letter/word sweep; line-only and unavailable lyrics retain upstream behavior rather than fabricating sung timing.
+Zunévio changes include distinct application/package identifiers, Amit Hasan Sami publisher metadata, Z icons, visible/export branding, Glass enabled by default for new Android installs, and a translucent lyric capsule connected to the actual player backdrop in both portrait and landscape layouts. Reduced-blur settings and unsupported-device fallbacks remain in place. Saved user preferences are not overwritten. Lyrics need a provider with word timestamps for the native letter/word sweep; line-only and unavailable lyrics retain upstream behavior rather than fabricating sung timing.
 
 The HTML in design-preview remains a separate interactive concept. It is not evidence that its entire custom layout has been ported to native code. The native UI deliberately retains BitChord's own layouts and animation implementation.
 
